# What a board can be made with: each entry is one way of making boards — etched at home, a board house's ordinary
# service, its fine-line one —, with the least copper, gaps and holes that way can make, and the tracks and vias a board
# made that way is laid with unless a net class says otherwise. A board names one (`rules standard`) and may tighten or
# loosen any value on its own line; a change of a house's capability is an edit here, never of a board.
#
# The least values are the ones a board's checks hold every track, via, pad and hole to — and a poured zone keeps no
# copper narrower than the least track —; the usual ones are what the editor lays new copper with. A zone joins a pad of
# its own net across the thermal gap by spokes this wide, so the pad can be soldered. The thicknesses are what copper
# analysis reads: a track's resistance and the current it carries follow its copper's thickness, a via's its plating and
# the board's thickness. 0.035 mm is 1 oz copper.
sheet "Board rules" as board-rules {
    description "The clearances, widths and holes a printed circuit board is checked against, by how it is made."
    source "The published capabilities of common prototype board houses, rounded to values every one of them makes"
    usual "standard"

    home "Etched at home — toner transfer or photoresist, drilled by hand" {
        clearance 0.4 mm
        least-track-width 0.4 mm
        least-drill 0.6 mm
        least-via-drill 0.8 mm
        least-via-ring 0.4 mm
        hole-clearance 0.5 mm
        edge-clearance 1 mm
        thermal-gap 0.6 mm
        thermal-spoke-width 0.8 mm
        track-width 0.8 mm
        via-drill 0.8 mm
        via-diameter 1.8 mm
        copper-thickness 0.035 mm
        inner-copper-thickness 0.035 mm
        plating-thickness 0.02 mm
        board-thickness 1.6 mm
    }

    standard "A board house's ordinary one- and two-layer service" {
        clearance 0.2 mm
        least-track-width 0.15 mm
        least-drill 0.3 mm
        least-via-drill 0.3 mm
        least-via-ring 0.15 mm
        hole-clearance 0.25 mm
        edge-clearance 0.3 mm
        thermal-gap 0.5 mm
        thermal-spoke-width 0.5 mm
        track-width 0.25 mm
        via-drill 0.4 mm
        via-diameter 0.8 mm
        copper-thickness 0.035 mm
        inner-copper-thickness 0.0175 mm
        plating-thickness 0.02 mm
        board-thickness 1.6 mm
    }

    fine "A board house's fine-line multilayer service" {
        clearance 0.1 mm
        least-track-width 0.1 mm
        least-drill 0.2 mm
        least-via-drill 0.2 mm
        least-via-ring 0.1 mm
        hole-clearance 0.2 mm
        edge-clearance 0.2 mm
        thermal-gap 0.3 mm
        thermal-spoke-width 0.3 mm
        track-width 0.15 mm
        via-drill 0.3 mm
        via-diameter 0.6 mm
        copper-thickness 0.035 mm
        inner-copper-thickness 0.0175 mm
        plating-thickness 0.025 mm
        board-thickness 1.6 mm
    }
}
